+Samples are assigned by forecast-origin index: origins \(t<t_{\mathrm{split}}\) enter the training pool and origins \(t\geq t_{\mathrm{split}}\) enter the test pool. The data are not shuffled. This construction makes fitting-target timestamps and test-target timestamps disjoint, but it does not insert a horizon-length purge between origin sets. At \(h=24\), the last training targets occur 23 retained positions after the first test origin and immediately before the first test target. The same no-purge rule is used between the fitting and validation origin sets. Consequently, the protocol is chronological by origin but is not a strict real-time, leakage-free backtest; all earlier blanket leakage-free wording has been removed.
 
