+\section{Cross-Series Aggregation for 24-Hour-Ahead Multi-Region Load Point Forecasting: A Component-Level Evaluation}\label{cross-series-aggregation-for-24-hour-ahead-multi-region-load-point-forecasting-a-component-level-evaluation}
+
+\textbf{Authors:} Jieyun Zheng (郑洁云), Linyao Zhang (张林垚), Zhanghuang Zhang (张章煌), Zhuolin Chen (陈卓琳), Ying Shi (施莹) \textbf{Affiliations:} Economic and Technological Research Institute of State Grid Fujian Electric Power Co., Ltd., Fuzhou 350000, Fujian, China \textbf{Correspondence:} zjy\_0701@163.com (J. Zheng)
+
+\subsection{Abstract}\label{abstract}
+
+Cross-correlated regional load series motivate graph and attention mechanisms, but single-run accuracy tables rarely isolate whether cross-series aggregation itself contributes. CSA-LoadNet combines a shared temporal encoder, cross-series attention, and a compact prediction head for multi-region load forecasting. The evaluated target is one scalar load value 24 retained hourly steps after each forecast origin. We call this a 24-hour-ahead point forecast, or day-ahead for brevity; it is not a 24-point next-day trajectory. Ten seeded runs under a chronological forecast-origin split show that, on the six-country Open Power System Data benchmark, the full model improves MAPE over a multilayer perceptron (0.0323 versus 0.0337; Holm-adjusted p = 0.0085) and over the no-aggregation ablation (0.0323 versus 0.0346; p = 0.0011). No difference among Poincaré, Euclidean, equal-weight, or fixed-distance-scale parameterizations is resolved at the available precision. We additionally rebuild Ausgrid as an exact 12-leaf, four-group, one-root hierarchy and evaluate independent, bottom-up, top-down, and OLS reconciliation with ten seeds for every method. DLinear with bottom-up reconciliation is best (hierarchy-weighted sMAPE 0.2802); CSA-LoadNet with OLS reaches 0.2895, while both coherent methods have zero structural violation. The resolved OPSD result concerns cross-series aggregation in this 24-step point task, not a particular geometry or a full next-day load path.
+
+\textbf{Keywords:} short-term load forecasting; 24-hour-ahead point forecasting; multi-region load; cross-series attention; ablation study; statistical significance testing; negative results; open power system data
 
